/// \class GiveUpgradeUpdate
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_b
/// \brief Special-ability update registered as "GiveUpgradeUpdate".
///
/// Its constructor starts with the SpecialAbilityUpdate constructor (see
/// the group page), so the module runs a special ability. Its data
/// (GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData) adds an effect, a spawn-out FX, a fade-out
/// speed and a switch for delivering the upgrade to the shared
/// special-ability fields. The name and fields suggest an ability that
/// hands an upgrade to a target and fades the giver out; this page does not
/// confirm the sequence. BFME 1 has the class; Zero Hour does not.
///
/// \see GiveUpgradeUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData, \ref page_core_frameworks_upgrades

/// \fn Module *GiveUpgradeUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "GiveUpgradeUpdate": creates the
///        module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration when an
/// object whose template lists the module is built. The group page
/// describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData for this
///                    module line, shared with every other object of the
///                    template.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see GiveUpgradeUpdate, GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_b
/// \brief Module data for GiveUpgradeUpdate: the shared special-ability
///        fields plus four of its own.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData. Its constructor
/// first runs the constructor that
/// SpecialAbilityUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData runs, taken to be
/// SpecialAbilityUpdateModuleData's constructor (a structural inference;
/// see the group page).
/// Its \c buildFieldParse registers SpecialAbilityUpdateModuleData's table
/// before its own.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields, read from the retail table: \c GiveUpgradeEffect and
/// \c SpawnOutFX, FX lists that are none by default; \c FadeOutSpeed, a
/// real number; and \c DeliverUpgrade, a boolean, false by default. The
/// special power the ability serves is named by the shared
/// \c SpecialPowerTemplate field (\ref page_core_frameworks_upgrades).
///
/// \see GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "GiveUpgradeUpdate": builds the
///        module data for one module line and parses its INI block.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration.
/// It constructs GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData with its defaults, then, when
/// \p ini is not null, parses the block with INI::initFromINIMultiProc and
/// GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData::buildFieldParse, so the block accepts the
/// shared special-ability fields and the class's own.
///
/// \param ini  The INI reader positioned at the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores,
///         or null when the allocation fails.
/// \see GiveUpgradeUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      GiveUpgradeUpdateModuleData


